// Party results — the William Tell gallop: a hard-light trumpet call, the galloping theme in E,
// original strains of galloping 16ths in A major and C# minor, and a cheeky key lift to G.
(
    title: "William Tell",
    composer: "Gioachino Rossini (1792-1868)",
    work: "Guillaume Tell (William Tell), Overture — IV. Finale, \"March of the Swiss Soldiers\" (1829)",
    source: "Trumpet call and gallop rhythm/opening of the finale theme from the public-domain score (written from memory, freely continued); the strains, harmony and arrangement are original to Brightest Day.",
